# The editor's top bar
Joined to the top of the window, with three sections:
the project's menu and the app's menus, then Run and Edit in the middle, then the tools and you.
What's in each is still the editor's own, `EditorToolbar` in `SpellEditor.tsx`:  each is a thing here that draws itself.

<spell-app "editor bar">
	<property "project menu" description="The project's menu:  Spell's hat, and its name">a thing</>
	<property "app menus" description="File, Edit, View, Run and Help">a thing</>
	<property "mode buttons" description="Run and Edit">a thing</>
	<property "tools" description="Inspect app and the Inspector's menu in Edit, then Restart and the theme">a thing</>
	<property "you" description="The person's own menu">a thing</>

	<draw>
		<ui-menu appearance="header" class="AppMenu tight EditorBar">
			<ui-menu position="left" class="third side">
				{draw its project menu}
				{draw its app menus}
				<ui-item class="spring no-border"/>
			</ui-menu>
			<ui-menu position="left" class="third">
				<ui-item class="spring no-border"/>
				{draw its mode buttons}
				<ui-item class="spring no-border"/>
			</ui-menu>
			<ui-menu position="right" class="third side BarTools">
				<ui-item class="spring no-border"/>
				<ui-menu appearance="capsule">
					{draw its tools}
				</ui-menu>
				{draw its you}
			</ui-menu>
		</ui-menu>
	</draw>
</spell-app>
